10. SENSORY RANGES IN RAPIDITY
======================================================================

  Each sense has a dynamic range between threshold and saturation.

  Sense                         Min        Max   Octaves
  -------------------------------------------------------
  Human hearing                  20     20,000      9.97
  Human vision                  400        700      0.81
  Dog hearing                    67     45,000      9.39
  Bat echolocation           20,000    200,000      3.32
  Elephant infrasound             1     12,000     13.55

  Human hearing spans ~10 octaves (20 Hz to 20 kHz).
  Human vision spans ~0.8 octaves (as we computed).
  Bats: ~3.3 octaves of echolocation.

  In rapidity: hearing range = 3.4539, vision range = 0.2798
  Hearing is 12.3x wider than vision in rapidity space.

======================================================================
GRAND SYNTHESIS: RAPIDITY IN BIOLOGY
======================================================================

  BIOLOGY                RAPIDITY IS                    KEY VALUE
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
  Species diversity      ln(#species)/2                 6.9 (insects)
  Genome size            ln(base pairs)/2               10.9 (human)
  Evolution timeline     ln(years ago)/2                2-11 (uniform!)
  Allometric scaling     LINEAR in rapidity             B ~ M^{3/4}
  Fibonacci growth       n * ln(phi)/2 per step         0.24/step
  Cell divisions         n * ln(2)/2 per doubling       0.35/doubling
  DNA sequence space     N * ln(4)/2                    1 octave/base
  Sensory range          ln(max/min)/2                  ~10 oct (hearing)
  Extinction severity    arctanh(2*survival - 1)        deeply negative

  Rapidity linearizes biological scaling laws.
  Evolution is approximately uniform in rapidity time.
  Each cell division adds one octave to the organism.
  Each DNA base adds one octave to sequence space.
